# SYNOPSIS

```usage
link target name
```

# DESCRIPTION

`link` calls `link` to make <name> a second name for the existing file <target>.
It takes no flags.
It is sbase's command, in `/boot/bin/posix`: the POSIX namespace (a manifest's `ns=posix`, made by `/lib/ns/posix`, see namespace(6)) binds that directory before `/boot/bin` on `/bin`, so a POSIX program finds it there.

# SEE ALSO

ln(1), unlink(1), link(5); sbase's page is `third_party/sbase/link.1` in the repository

# DIAGNOSTICS

A failure is reported as `link: link: ` and the error, and the exit status is 1; success is 0.
Anything but two arguments prints the usage message and exits 1.

# BUGS

No VectraOS file server has hard links, and the C library's `link` fails with `EPERM` without asking one (see link(5)), so `link` always fails, with `Operation not permitted`.
